{"answer":"To stop Python from showing the original exception as the cause when raising a new one, you can specify `None` in the `from` clause of the `raise` statement. For example:

```python
try:
    print(1 / 0)
except:
    raise RuntimeError("Something bad happened") from None
```

This will suppress the context of the original exception, resulting in a traceback that only shows the new exception [B:py3.11/raise#1:c003].","citations":["B:py3.11/raise#1:c003"],"abstain":false}
